{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.323176Z","id":"94aa7d913252b8b216c542489d7feea9d020c60bf00feb00be2338ef976adb91","body":{"detail":"Anyone may send a victim /signin/<their own code>; the button then signs the victim's browser in as the sender (login CSRF by persuasion: what the victim then writes lands in the sender's account). The page shows no name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"c6aaf5f6ac5c50bf4f5ab6413f0e00eeb7c06848183bbc03aec9fc59e2daedf7"},"suggested_fix":"Peek the link (as GET /api/hosted/invites/<code> peeks an invite) and show 'Sign in as <name>'.","summary":"The sign-in link page does not say whose account it signs into","tags":["hosted","security","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/HostedPanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.323279Z","id":"60305d91cc5cc0059cf32889f0b09cf6b5419695888c23b7c2328d83385237f8","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/hosted/artifacts/<aid>/link answers 403 forbidden for a page the person did not make (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs set_link); the panel lists listArtifacts() whole and shows the refusal after the click.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"3752682700ce76a13362ae7dae9c8f65d7eafd4c8cb7e5069c9547fd9b1a1113"},"suggested_fix":"List only pages the person made (or the owner every page).","summary":"People's share picker offers a person every page they can read, though they may share only those they made","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372562Z","id":"d0c2bd91e3ea98aae28ae0602ec28dc8b725f08e5b6faaa1b00aac0d9b21eda1","body":{"detail":"The /signin/<code> page offers 'Sign in on this device' without naming the person, and crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs accept_signin_link and accept_invite end the browser's current session (end_replaced). Any member can mint a sign-in link for themselves and send it to another member: one click signs the victim's browser in as the attacker, and the victim's later comments, approvals, uploads and publishes land as the attacker's (login CSRF). Redemption needs the click, and a sandboxed page cannot do it (its popups send Origin: null).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"2195fa29e587cbcacec135e50c2bab0738b09a6199734ce3cab4061a228c22a8"},"suggested_fix":"Add a rate-limited peek of a sign-in link (as for invites) so the page names the person, and when the browser is signed in as someone else, say that continuing signs them out.","summary":"Redeeming a sign-in link or an invite replaces the browser's session without saying as whom it signs in","tags":["security","hosted","web","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:58:51.049005Z","id":"f0763aee54b4f37d812986d676c5766949287989d4ce0d85e6433727aab6058f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:65f84006","summary":"The /signin/<code> page names the link's member (GET /api/hosted/signin-links/<code>, Store::peek_signin_link) and its button reads 'Sign in as <name>'. cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_hosted: 35 passed, including a_sign_in_link_says_whose_account_it_is_and_replaces_a_session_only_when_confirmed and an_invite_replaces_a_browsers_session_only_when_confirmed; npx playwright test hosted.spec.ts: 3 passed (the owner's browser opening Sam's link sees 'You are signed in here as Ada, the owner. Signing in as Sam signs you out of Ada.' and an unconfirmed POST answers 409 session_exists).","supersedes":"94aa7d913252b8b216c542489d7feea9d020c60bf00feb00be2338ef976adb91","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:58:51.056689Z","id":"57efb9155d139dced7e86b1e97fcaf35a947e1bd5345465f86a5f5dd1980567d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:65f84006","summary":"accept_signin_link and accept_invite answer 409 session_exists (naming the current person, spending nothing) while the browser holds a live session of someone else, unless the body is {\"replace\": true}; the pages say who the browser is signed in as and that the click signs them out, and send replace with it. cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_hosted: 35 passed, including a_sign_in_link_says_whose_account_it_is_and_replaces_a_session_only_when_confirmed and an_invite_replaces_a_browsers_session_only_when_confirmed; npx playwright test hosted.spec.ts: 3 passed (the owner's browser opening Sam's link sees 'You are signed in here as Ada, the owner. Signing in as Sam signs you out of Ada.' and an unconfirmed POST answers 409 session_exists).","supersedes":"d0c2bd91e3ea98aae28ae0602ec28dc8b725f08e5b6faaa1b00aac0d9b21eda1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/HostedPanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.168284Z","id":"2453bd8bfda2fa812c0871fcc2c163f7dc05a734afea30f5138bba96362c1ca4","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/hosted/artifacts/<aid>/link answers 403 forbidden for a page the person did not make (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs set_link); the panel lists listArtifacts() whole and shows the refusal after the click.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"3752682700ce76a13362ae7dae9c8f65d7eafd4c8cb7e5069c9547fd9b1a1113"},"suggested_fix":"List only pages the person made (or the owner every page).","summary":"People's share picker offers a person every page they can read, though they may share only those they made","supersedes":"60305d91cc5cc0059cf32889f0b09cf6b5419695888c23b7c2328d83385237f8","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:59:16.483089Z","id":"8ad16a99436c0851a7c7dcb3562cac742405baf97a3a947609463f8534224bd9","body":{"detail":"The <code> holding the user code has no white-space: nowrap, so where the sentence happens to end near the card's edge the code splits at its dash: at 1280 px with client_name \"Clax on Pixel\", the Clax app's sentence (\", the Clax app,\") renders \"ZKMM-\" on one line and \"5473\" on the next (web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts test \"the Clax app signs in by device code\", shots device-app-1280-light/dark). The person is asked to compare this code with the device's; a split code is harder to check. Phone width happened to keep it whole.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":177},"end":{"line":177},"content_hash":"16dbc0260c5556147a57078274c59b80b13f4fbbfdeb50ad16ee5d052e5992de"},"suggested_fix":"white-space: nowrap on .signin code (or the user-code element alone).","summary":"The device approval page breaks the user code across two lines at desktop width","tags":["ux","hosted","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/HostedPanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:06:53.788214Z","id":"291bba5931b426f25e4f5a15c6b0c623832d49ab5b6b5857066903f533594f1e","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/hosted/artifacts/<aid>/link answers 403 forbidden for a page the person did not make (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs set_link); the panel lists listArtifacts() whole and shows the refusal after the click.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":42},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"3752682700ce76a13362ae7dae9c8f65d7eafd4c8cb7e5069c9547fd9b1a1113"},"suggested_fix":"List only pages the person made (or the owner every page).","summary":"People's share picker offers a person every page they can read, though they may share only those they made","supersedes":"2453bd8bfda2fa812c0871fcc2c163f7dc05a734afea30f5138bba96362c1ca4","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:06:59.373122Z","id":"ba7b998bb2a7fe80f303cb19d9b7a4601a4d449e17a8a1850490053cbff4e903","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ce4f4a67a","summary":"The user code no longer wraps: .signin code has white-space: nowrap; the e2e screenshot device-app-1280-light (CLAX_E2E_SHOTS run of //web:e2e_rest, PASSED) shows GNCL-6310 on one line at 1280 and 390 px","supersedes":"8ad16a99436c0851a7c7dcb3562cac742405baf97a3a947609463f8534224bd9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:46:42.497066Z","id":"6d6de2b39c44da7aca9ae3de9728ab479bec4ba756e0d3c7bf74213efbc57fd0","body":{"detail":"The hint reads \"As the Clax app, it may also change who can see the pages you made ... and whether anyone may comment on them.\" A person-device token reaches PUT /api/hosted/artifacts/<aid>/shares (crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs PERSON_DEVICE_ROUTES), which takes access viewer, commenter or editor (crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs ShareAccess::parse), so the device can make someone an editor of a page the person made (or, for the owner, of any page). \"Who can see\" reads as view access only. web/shell/src/hosted/HostedPanel.svelte:84 (the Devices note) has the same wording.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":179},"end":{"line":179},"content_hash":"c9d5e5435abec638f787ef92e0e64ed9bbbb53010b40dbbc29dc87e7ef02f800"},"suggested_fix":"\"change who can see or edit the pages you made\" (on the approval page and the Devices note).","summary":"The Clax app's approval text says it may change who can see the pages, but it may also give people edit access to them","tags":["ux","hosted","review","security","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:03:30.510839Z","id":"cfc9b2752b5c8cfc8a2973c8311bd03403e1ea74ee1d12b03365d28d7ca37409","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5072ade58","summary":"The approval page (SignIn.svelte:179) and the People Devices note (HostedPanel.svelte:84) now say the app may change who can see or edit the pages; SignIn.test.ts, HostedPanel.test.ts and the hosted.spec.ts:449 e2e assert it: bazelisk test //web:unit PASSED, //web:e2e_rest PASSED","supersedes":"6d6de2b39c44da7aca9ae3de9728ab479bec4ba756e0d3c7bf74213efbc57fd0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:23:01.150908Z","id":"9c4bb7245860d005f0c4863820168fd02b92557c5a703174012cace393a68d62","body":{"detail":"The hint reads 'It gets an agent token of yours: what it publishes is public as yours, within your rights.' for every device sign-in, a clax-app one included (web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.test.ts pins the sentence for clax-app). docs/contract.md:3375-3376 and docs/usage.md:317-318 say an app's first publish goes up Restricted, only its owner, with comments off. A person approving their phone reads that what it publishes is public.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":179},"end":{"line":179},"content_hash":"cebde45afb2b8e7983e884678209b670ba9ba31a8dcae12d6a7dad144c5458a5"},"suggested_fix":"For isApp, say 'what it publishes is yours, within your rights; an app it publishes stays private until you share it' (or drop 'public' for both kinds), and update SignIn.test.ts and web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts.","summary":"The device approval page tells the person the Clax app's publishes are 'public as yours', but the app's first publish is Restricted","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:25:21.801372Z","id":"8535a8a7cd2f0e577fbcca62b2350cec440abdb2c4788fc4ac1cfb0e3d2fa4a6","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte:179 renders 'what it publishes is public as yours' outside the {#if isApp} block, so it shows for a clax-app device; web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.test.ts:27 and web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts:462 pin it. docs/contract.md:3375-3376 'A first publish makes the copy Restricted, with comments off'; docs/usage.md:316-317 'The app goes up Restricted, only you until you share it'.","kind":"comment","references":"9c4bb7245860d005f0c4863820168fd02b92557c5a703174012cace393a68d62","summary":"confirmed: the hint says 'public as yours' for the Clax app too, whose first publish is Restricted","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:54.117217Z","id":"d8a4701690003f7d98b6a09133e042b4ddf0b2a11ab0babbd8264724061bcad6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c48bf2cee","summary":"For the Clax app the hint reads 'what it publishes is yours, within your rights, and an app it publishes stays private until you share it.'; another machine's Clax keeps 'public as yours'. web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.test.ts pins both and that the app's page lacks 'public as yours'; web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts:462 pins the app's. //web:unit passes and //web:e2e_rest with e2e/hosted.spec.ts passes ('the Clax app signs in by device code...'). Mutation: the old SignIn.svelte fails 'tells the person the Clax app may manage the sharing of their apps'.","supersedes":"9c4bb7245860d005f0c4863820168fd02b92557c5a703174012cace393a68d62","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/Landing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:13:46.717118Z","id":"468cf610e4af7771fababd6d66ca37880513b096259b0bb66aaec4abd992c9d3","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/hosted/Landing.test.ts checks the header, the frame's src and the button in jsdom, and the landing chunk is in the built shell; nothing loads /start/ in Chromium to see the frame fill the page, the quickstart's target=_top links leave it, or the reel play in it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":20},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"390a0ca150c7a3bf11238ea882513338e92a66f7e48f49ddfd358fe1e9ab03ba"},"summary":"No browser test covers /start/'s chrome around the quickstart frame","tags":["test-coverage","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/hosted/HostedPanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:39.012406Z","id":"bb8dd029e582925c256a7991a5082081ee2cdf8146850d94a01b615aa1a33d8e","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/hosted/artifacts/<aid>/link answers 403 forbidden for a page the person did not make (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs set_link); the panel lists listArtifacts() whole and shows the refusal after the click.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"3752682700ce76a13362ae7dae9c8f65d7eafd4c8cb7e5069c9547fd9b1a1113"},"suggested_fix":"List only pages the person made (or the owner every page).","summary":"People's share picker offers a person every page they can read, though they may share only those they made","supersedes":"291bba5931b426f25e4f5a15c6b0c623832d49ab5b6b5857066903f533594f1e","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
